FEATURE PLAYTEST RULE:

After a feature checkpoint is reached, perform ONE focused Play-mode validation for that feature and its immediate integration points.

Do not perform a Play test for every individual implementation step that contributed to that feature.

Do not perform a Play test before the feature is sufficiently assembled to produce meaningful gameplay evidence, unless an earlier runtime test is specifically required to diagnose an otherwise unobservable blocker.

BATCHING RULE:

While implementing one feature, batch compatible fixes together.

For example:

IMPLEMENT FEATURE
→ DISCOVER 8 CODE ISSUES
→ FIX ALL 8 ISSUES
→ VALIDATE STATICALLY
→ INTEGRATE
→ ENTER PLAY MODE ONCE
→ VALIDATE THE FEATURE

NOT:

IMPLEMENT ONE CHANGE
→ PLAY

FIX ONE WARNING
→ PLAY

FIX ONE ERROR
→ PLAY

CHANGE ONE CONFIG VALUE
→ PLAY

REFACTOR ONE FUNCTION
→ PLAY

CONTINUE BATCHING UNTIL THE FEATURE CHECKPOINT IS READY.

BUG-FIX RETEST RULE:

If a feature Play test fails, DO NOT start a new Play session after every individual fix.

Instead:

1. Exit Play mode.
2. Collect and classify the failures discovered by the Play test.
3. Fix all currently known failures that belong to that feature.
4. Perform static, structural, configuration, and dependency validation.
5. Re-enter Play mode once to revalidate the repaired feature.
6. Repeat this fix-batch → single-retest cycle only when the previous feature-level Play test still fails.

This prevents a single bad Play test from turning every small corrective edit into another full Play session.

